@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security;architecture] explore-is-public-with-an-owned-lifetime
Explore MUST show anonymous Popular/search and public repository PR pages without
Access credentials or account sign-in. It MUST consume only the explicit tokenless
public client, never legacy Inbox/review stores or AI authority. Its route state MUST
cancel replaced requests, ignore stale results/errors and reject retired callbacks;
source retirement MUST clear inputs and rows. A popped public page MAY retain inert
rows only through its exit animation; popped callbacks/results MUST already be revoked.
Public repository selection and pagination MUST
retain the selected immutable repository ID, and a confirmed visibility/identity denial
MUST clear prior PR rows. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 signed-out browsing and personal
GitHub request, approved direct-native guest slice and public-boundary review.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] fresh-entry-does-not-inherit-a-private-workspace
A fresh/reinstalled native app without matching verified existing-connection evidence
MUST open Explore, even if a restored preference selected the existing-server entry.
A legitimate returning connection MUST retain its existing workspace unless the user
chose public browsing or Android's built-in staging GitHub entry applies. That choice
MUST preserve the saved private account. The built-in staging app MUST select GitHub's
public entry before confirmation instead of restoring the legacy email gate, and MUST
show its GitHub introduction once on migration; explicit custom-server connections
retain their compatibility entry. Source for this exception: Tavi's 25 Oct 2026 build397
email-sign-in screenshot and sole GitHub-login request. Selecting
another entry MUST revoke retained callbacks and pending results before mounting its
pages; returning to Explore MUST NOT revive a previous guest source. Public startup
MUST NOT instantiate private Home, account discovery, AI or Stats observers. Source:
Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 reinstall screenshot and no-sign-in public browsing request.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;security] guest-links-keep-public-and-private-authority-separate
Guest links MUST use the same Compose navigation stack and MUST NOT mount private
review/repository clients. A verified-format github.com PR link MUST open the read-only
public review (public-pull-requests-open-in-pully); other verified-format GitHub links
MAY offer an explicit fixed-origin Open on GitHub action. Private/server links
MUST offer the existing-account entry or public browsing without fetching private data.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 public browsing decision, nav-links-inside-open-like-outside,
the approved staged public list/PR implementation and recording 23 Oct 12:12, 00:50 to 01:12.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design;architecture] explore-reuses-pully-and-the-shared-stack
Android and iOS MUST use the same Explore state and presentation, Pully's existing
design kit and the host's shared Compose route stack. Opening a repository MUST use
the host navigation callback; Explore MUST NOT create an independent native/child
back stack. Public PR rows open inside Pully and MUST NOT be labelled as opening
GitHub (recording 23 Oct 12:12, 00:50 to 01:12). Account invitations MUST reflect real server
sign-in capability rather than inventing OAuth success or sending operator secrets.
Public PR list titles MUST keep the existing two-line ellipsis limit; ordinary
sheet labels MUST retain their full wrapping (android-whole-identifiers).
Source: mobile-reuses-production-ui, shared-navigation-keeps-one-compose-stack and
Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 guest browsing/personal sign-in request.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] guest-incoming-links-commit-before-consumption
A valid guest arrival MUST remain pending while its existing sheets close. Only a
current, uncancelled guest source holding that same pending arrival MAY append its
route and then consume it. A replaced arrival or retired source MUST NOT navigate
or consume its successor. Source: shared-navigation-keeps-one-compose-stack and the
22 Oct 2026 Compound guest link review.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] explore-refresh-keeps-known-content
Unknown public list content MUST use the existing skeletons rather than loading text
or a spinner. Returning to the foreground MUST quietly revalidate only the active
public page, coalescing an in-flight request and retaining its query, known rows and
loaded pagination until a complete current answer replaces them. A confirmed
repository visibility/identity denial MUST still clear its prior PR rows. Explore
MUST NOT expose a Refresh action or refresh indicator. Source: android-no-loading-screens,
android-refresh-is-silent and the 22 Oct 2026 guest contract review.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] explore-is-the-repositories
The Explore page is its title, an account button and the repositories: Popular or the
search results, then the search field. The intro, Connect GitHub and Use an existing
Pully account MUST live in a bottom sheet the account button opens, shown by itself
once on a fresh install and then only on request ("we would open a bottom sheet with
these things", recording 23 Oct 12:12, 00:26 to 00:30). The sheet MUST say so when
GitHub sign-in is not set up on the server rather than offer a button that fails.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security;architecture] public-pull-requests-open-in-pully
Tapping a public PR in Explore, or a github.com PR link in guest mode, MUST open Pully's
own review page, never GitHub ("if I click on one of these, I am taken to GitHub ... make
it so that those for sure do not open in GitHub", recording 23 Oct 12:12, 00:50 to 01:12).
It is read-only: it MUST read only tokenless HTTPS api.github.com GETs through its own
transport and session cache, carry no Pully server, Access, session or personal GitHub
credential, refuse every write, AI or private RPC with a sign-in message, and keep reads
for a few minutes to spare GitHub's hourly limit. A repository GitHub reports as private,
a redirect or a rate limit MUST end the read with the fixed public-browsing errors.
